% Bowel Management Devices: LCD L36267 and its Policy Article A54516 (DME
% MACs), read with NCD 280.1 (the Durable Medical Equipment Reference
% List). A policy program of the DMEPOS model: it includes dmepos.le
% (orders, delivery, benefit category, continued need, refills) and states
% when a claim for a bowel management device is REASONABLE AND NECESSARY:
% a bed pan (the standard E0275, the fracture pan E0276) for a beneficiary
% who is bed-confined. The benefits are the Article's: the bed pans are
% durable medical equipment (used in a home, dmepos.le), the rectal insert
% (A4337) a prosthetic device — but the LCD denies it as not reasonable and
% necessary ("they do not meet the medical evidence requirements"), so no
% rule concludes it. The devices the Article says fall under no benefit are
% in scope and in no benefit category: the gravity enema system (A4458),
% the pulsed irrigation and evacuation system and its supplies (E0350,
% E0352), the disposable sheets and bags (A4335), the underpads (A4553,
% A4554) and the diapers (A4520) — a claim for one fails at applicability.
% The policy has no documentation requirements of its own (the Article
% states none).
%
% How the criteria are read. That the beneficiary is bed-confined is a
% clinical judgment of the record, the one finding this policy reads (the
% judged template of dmepos.le, "the finding F about B is established" or
% unsupported, with who found it and why):
%   confined to bed (LCD: "Bed Pans (E0275, E0276) are covered for
%   beneficiaries who are bed-confined"; NCD 280.1: "Covered if patient is
%   bed confined").
% That the bed pan is durable is carried by its code (a disposable pan is
% billed as A9270, the generic noncovered code no policy of the model
% decides).
%
% Not modelled, and doubts. The transanal irrigation systems (A4459, the
% electronic A4479, the rectal catheter A4453): the Article places them in
% the Prosthetic Devices benefit and describes their coding, but the text
% of the LCD in sources/ states no coverage criterion for them — they are
% left out of the scope, so the model decides nothing about them (a claim
% for one is outside the model). The Article cites §1861(s)(9) for the
% prosthetic devices (the other Articles of the model cite §1861(s)(8)).
% The Article says it lists ICD-10 codes, but no table of them is in
% sources/icd10. Not modelled either: the electrical continence aids (no
% HCPCS code in either text; denied as experimental by the LCD); the fecal
% collection systems and their rectal catheters (no code named); the
% vaginal insert A4563 (not DME MAC jurisdiction).

the target language is: prolog.

the knowledge base bowel_management includes these resources:
    dmepos.

the knowledge base bowel_management includes:

LCD L36267 is published at "https://www.cms.gov/medicare-coverage-database/view/lcd.aspx?lcdid=36267".
the text of LCD L36267 is at "sources/lcd/L36267.txt".
Policy Article A54516 is published at "https://www.cms.gov/medicare-coverage-database/view/article.aspx?articleid=54516".
the text of Policy Article A54516 is at "sources/article/A54516.txt".
NCD 280 1 is published at "https://www.cms.gov/medicare-coverage-database/view/ncd.aspx?ncdid=190".
the text of NCD 280 1 is at "sources/ncd/NCD_280.1.txt".

% The codes this policy decides — outside the section checklist: a claim
% of another policy fails here without failing its own applicability.
% The codes this policy decides — the bed pans, the rectal insert, and the
% devices the Article places in no benefit — and their benefits: durable
% medical equipment for the bed pans, a prosthetic device for the rectal
% insert (Policy Article A54516).
rule bowel_codes with provenance Policy Article A54516,
        confer "Many bowel management devices (see bulleted list below, not all inclusive) fail one or more of the relevant requirements in §1861(n) of the Act and are thus statutorily excluded from coverage":
the policy for code a code is bowel_management
    if the code is in ["E0275", "E0276", "A4337", "A4458", "E0350", "E0352", "A4335", "A4520", "A4553", "A4554"].

section applicability is:

rule bowel_benefit_bed_pans with provenance Policy Article A54516,
        confer "Bed pans are covered under the Durable Medical Equipment benefit (Social Security Act §1861(s)(6))":
the benefit category of code a code is durable medical equipment
    if the code is in ["E0275", "E0276"].

rule bowel_benefit_rectal_insert with provenance Policy Article A54516,
        confer "Rectal inserts, electrical incontinence aids, and transanal irrigation (TAI) systems (which are comprised of a TAI device and rectal catheter that has a sealing function [balloon or cone-based]) are covered under the Prosthetic Devices benefit":
the benefit category of code a code is prosthetic devices
    if the code is "A4337".

bowel_management has no specific documentation requirements.

section question is:

% A bed pan: for a bed-confined beneficiary. The rectal insert has no rule:
% "Rectal inserts and related accessories (A4337) will be denied as not
% reasonable and necessary because they do not meet the medical evidence
% requirements outlined in the CMS Pub. 100-08, Medicare Program Integrity
% Manual (PIM), Chapter 13."
rule bowel_bed_pan with provenance LCD L36267,
        confer "Bed Pans (E0275, E0276) are covered for beneficiaries who are bed-confined":
a claim is reasonable and necessary
    if the claim is for an item
    and the HCPCS code of the item is a code
    and the code is in ["E0275", "E0276"]
    and the item is furnished to a beneficiary
    and the finding confined to bed about the beneficiary is established.
